1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,810
Start with an empty canvas. Add the DeepJEB geometry dataset.

2
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:19,410
Browse a real training shape before choosing a model.

3
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:25,390
Add SDFFlow: a learned shape representation and a conditional flow.

4
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:40,240
Set a batch size of one, and choose the training schedule.

5
00:00:40,240 --> 00:01:12,440
Use fresh output paths so this demo starts from scratch.

6
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:17,000
Connect the dataset output to the model training input.

7
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Click Train. Studio checks the configuration and launches the native trainer.

8
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,520
Training is now running. The training wait is omitted in the next edit.

9
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:37,820
Training demo stopped. Continue with previously trained SDFFlow and HI-MGN models.

10
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:47,880
Other model families are available in the same Studio.

11
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:56,010
Open the completed candidate run and choose a bracket.

12
00:01:56,010 --> 00:02:00,300
The stress field is a HI-MGN prediction. Drag to inspect it in 3D.

13
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:09,520
Change the field to vertical displacement on the same shape.

14
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:17,600
Choose the candidate table and compare mass with vertical deflection.

15
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:30,230
Try a 0.4 mm deflection constraint and keep five selected designs.

16
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:38,770
The Pareto front shows the mass-deflection trade-off. Click a design.
